                    insight_recovered:      `Curve bent: you read the crisis as ambiguous and reduced that ambiguity — empathy plus credible evidence, genuine WOM amplified, paid media sequenced after the page converted, and the banner kept off. Sentiment recovered, reach was contained, conversion climbed back, and ROI cleared 1×. You defended the word-of-mouth moat by trusting it, not faking it.`,
                    insight_astroturf:      `Moat burned: manufacturing fake reviews tripped the marketplace's fraud detection, purged the reviews and suspended the listing — converting a rumor crisis into a policy violation and proving the accuser's point that you game reviews. The trust asset the whole brand was built on is the one you destroyed defending it.`,
                    insight_silence:        `Silence calcified: staying quiet let reach double to ~4.8 million, the journalist published “did not respond,” and the marketplace added the precautionary banner. Ambiguity left unresolved hardened into common knowledge no later rebuttal could dislodge. Silence didn't let it die — it let the rumor become the only story.`,
                    insight_paidearly:      `Paid the wrong page: you spent on visibility before repairing sentiment, so shoppers saw the ad, read the 1-star pile-on and bounced. ROI stayed below 1× because you paid to drive traffic to a page that converted skeptics into non-buyers. Trust repair sequences before paid amplification — every time.`,
                    insight_legalism:       `Legalism over empathy: leading with legal threats answered the accuser and dismissed the genuinely worried customers, who felt lawyered-at instead of answered. For an ambiguous scare, evidence with empathy resolves the doubt; a legal posture just amplifies it.`,
                    insight_mixed:          `A partial recovery: some moves landed, but the posture, the WOM play, the sequencing and the week-2 response didn't fully reinforce each other — enough seams for the rumor to keep some of its reach and for the KPIs to fall short of a clean save.`,
                    insight_dismissed:      `You treated genuine concern as an attack: branding the whole wave a smear alienated the ~40% who were real worried buyers — the advocates you needed for the WOM drive. The diagnostic discipline Sudhir's research demands is telling a coordinated pile-on from a real concern and answering each correctly.`,
                    insight_conversion_low: `Hero-SKU conversion never climbed back near 6.8%: the bleed kept running because the page still reads as risky to shoppers. Conversion is the truest signal that trust was actually repaired — impressions and statements don't move it; a believable page does.`,
                    insight_reach_high:     `Rumor reach stayed high: the spread was never contained at its hubs early enough, so the doubling curve outran your response and the rumor kept finding new audiences.`,
                    insight_roi_low:        `Sentiment and conversion recovered, but ROI stayed under 1×: too much budget went to paid media relative to the cheap, high-trust repair levers, or paid ran before the page was ready. The sequencing — and the mix — is what leadership judges.`,
                    insight_sequenced:      `You sequenced it right: trust repair first, paid amplification second, a reserve held for the second wave, and honest reporting at the end. That ordering is the single biggest ROI lever in a reputation crisis — and the one most teams get backwards.`,

                    hint_astroturf:         `The fake-review drive tripped fraud detection and suspended the listing — ROI is capped and the moat is burned. There is no recovering this with more spend; the only lesson left is why the integrity line was non-negotiable.`,
                    hint_silence:           `Silence let reach explode and the banner go up. Break the silence now with empathy and credible evidence — but the rumor has hardened, and a later rebuttal moves the curve far less than an early one would have.`,
                    hint_paidearly:         `You're paying to amplify a page customers distrust — ROI is stuck below 1×. Shift budget into the repair levers (advocates, community, PR, the lab landing page) and let conversion recover before you scale paid.`,
                    hint_reach:             `Rumor reach is still climbing — you haven't contained it at the hubs. Cut the spread at the 120k-follower video and the WhatsApp forwards, and reduce the ambiguity feeding the shares.`,
                    hint_dismissed:         `You branded the whole wave a smear and lost the genuine advocates. Re-engage the ~40% of worried buyers as customers, not enemies, before the WOM drive can work.`,
                    hint_sentiment:         `Net sentiment is dangerously low. Reduce the ambiguity with empathy and a credible lab certificate, and amplify genuine voices — out-shouting the rumor won't move it.`,
                    hint_strong:            `Strong position — sentiment recovered, conversion climbing, reach contained. Land it: document the response, apply your kill/scale triggers, and pitch the CEO on all four KPIs.`,

